{title: 586 - What Joy It Is to Worship Here}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #586 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 586}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]What [G]joy it is to [D]worship here,
[Am]And find ourselves [G]at home,
[D7/C]Where [Am]God, who uses [D7]every gift,
[G]Has room for all who come!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Yet [G]are no two of [D]us alike
[Am]Of all the [G/D]human race,
[D7/C]And [Am]we must seek [D7]a common ground
[G]If we would share His grace.
{end_of_verse}
